# Database Schema (Supabase / PostgreSQL)

## Tables

### users
| Column     | Type                     | Notes                                      |
|------------|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| id         | uuid (PK)                | DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()                   |
| name       | varchar NOT NULL          |                                             |
| email      | varchar NOT NULL UNIQUE   |                                             |
| role       | varchar NOT NULL          | CHECK: 'admin', 'parent', 'child'           |
| password   | varchar(6) DEFAULT NULL   | 6-character login password (nullable)       |
| status     | varchar DEFAULT 'active'  | CHECK: 'active', 'inactive'                 |
| created_at | timestamptz DEFAULT now() |                                             |
| updated_at | timestamptz DEFAULT now() |                                             |

### permissions
Only 3 rows: **fan**, **light**, **door**

| Column      | Type                     | Notes                    |
|-------------|--------------------------|--------------------------|
| id          | uuid (PK)                | DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()|
| name        | varchar NOT NULL UNIQUE   | 'fan', 'light', 'door'  |
| description | text                     |                          |
| created_at  | timestamptz DEFAULT now() |                          |

### user_permissions
Each user has one row per permission with `granted` = true/false.

| Column        | Type                     | Notes                          |
|---------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------|
| id            | uuid (PK)                | DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()      |
| user_id       | uuid FK → users.id       |                                |
| permission_id | uuid FK → permissions.id |                                |
| granted       | boolean DEFAULT true     | true = allowed, false = denied |
| created_at    | timestamptz DEFAULT now() |                                |
| updated_at    | timestamptz DEFAULT now() |                                |

### voice_recordings
| Column        | Type                     | Notes                                              |
|---------------|--------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| id            | uuid (PK)                | DEFAULT gen_random_uuid()                           |
| user_id       | uuid FK → users.id       |                                                    |
| storage_path  | varchar NOT NULL          | Legacy; new uploads use audio_base64 instead        |
| audio_base64  | text                     | Base64-encoded 16kHz mono WAV audio data            |
| duration_ms   | integer                  |                                                    |
| language      | varchar                  |                                                    |
| transcription | text                     |                                                    |
| command_type  | varchar                  |                                                    |
| status        | varchar DEFAULT 'uploaded'| CHECK: 'uploaded','processing','processed','failed' |
| created_at    | timestamptz DEFAULT now() |                                                    |
| processed_at  | timestamptz               |                                                    |
| section_id    | varchar                  |                                                    |
| section_title | varchar                  |                                                    |
| repetition    | integer                  |                                                    |

## Permission Model
- There are exactly 3 permissions: `fan`, `light`, `door`
- Each user gets a row in `user_permissions` per permission
- `granted = true` means the user can control that device
- `granted = false` means access is denied
- If no row exists for a user+permission, default is `true`

## Supabase Client
- URL: configured in `src/lib/supabase.js`
- The app uses `@supabase/supabase-js` via React Native
